{
  "_comment": "The name a file gets when it reaches an upload without a real one (2026-11-17, docs/CHANNEL_FILES.md §4.4): pasted images, the camera, photo-library pictures that lose their name, placeholders. Name: <kind>_<yyyyMMdd>_<HHmmss>[_<n>].<ext> in the device's local time (Gregorian, ASCII digits) when the file is added; ext lower-cased, no dot when there is none. index: the 2nd, 3rd … unnamed file added in the same second (any kind) gets _2, _3 …; the first has none. kind: photo (camera, photo library), image (other unnamed pictures, pasted images), video, file; kinds maps a MIME type to one (image/* → image, video/* → video, else file; case-insensitive). unnamed: names that count as no name (trimmed, ASCII case-insensitive): empty, file, image.<image ext> and photo.<image ext> (image ext: png jpg jpeg gif webp heic heif tif tiff bmp avif), video.<video ext> (mov mp4 m4v webm). Desktop / Web rename these only for pasted and dropped files; a picked file keeps its name whatever it is. Hand-written; desktop (tests/uploadNames.test.ts), iOS (UploadNamesTests) and Android (UploadNamesTest) read this file.",
